__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.venv-mcp/
.venv-laya/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
coverage.json
htmlcov/
htmlcov/

# Runtime data (generated by ETL/analytics)
# NOTE: analysis/ and export/ are SOURCE packages (analysis/*.py,
# export/pbix_export.py, export/BaseThemes/). Only their generated output is
# ignored below. Blanket-ignoring them left ~56 source files untracked, so a
# clone could not import the analysis layer or the Power BI export engine.
data/
logs/
outputs/
analysis/audit/

# Build & packaging artifacts
dist/
dist-verify2/
build/

# Local change backups
backups/

# Stray artefacts that used to sit at the repo root (see docs/LAUNCH-FIX-PLAN.md
# item R6). `out.html` was a stale copy of the SPA shell, `ollama` was a
# 0-byte file, `lib/` was an empty directory. All three are build noise.
/out.html
/ollama
/lib/

# Browser-automation scratch (Playwright MCP console logs + page snapshots)
.playwright-mcp/

# A throwaway low-privilege copy of the Inno Setup script, used to verify the
# installer's payload without elevation. Never shipped, never committed.
installers/DataAgentTest.iss

# Graphify analysis cache
agent/graphify-out/
# The graphify knowledge graph is a regenerable tool artifact (~233 MB, mostly
# duplicate dated snapshots of the same graph). It is useful locally but is a
# liability in a repo whose pitch is "read the whole stack before you approve
# it" — a multi-hundred-MB clone is the first thing an evaluator hits.
# Regenerate with: graphify update .
graphify-out/
*.exe
*.msi
*.whl
*.zip
linux-install.zip
linux-install/
# Third-party binaries fetched at build time, never committed.
installers/opencode/

# An archive OF this project is never a source artefact. A .rar/.zip of the
# working tree carries config/users.json (password hashes + plaintext API
# keys), data/.jwt_secret, data/.grant_key, the warehouse and .env - every
# file the list above exists to keep out of git. A 1.9 GB
# DataAgent-public.rar was found sitting in the working tree during the
# pre-launch review; it is deleted, and these patterns stop it coming back.
*.rar
*.7z
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
/DataAgent-public.*
/shots/

# Runtime config state (keep *.yaml config seeds)
config/users.json
config/db_connections.json
config/google_login_pending.json
config/google_login_pending/
config/llm_runtime.json
config/revoked_jtis.json

# Editor / OS
.vscode/*
!.vscode/mcp.json
.idea/
.vs/
*.suo
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Agent harness internals
.ecc/
.hermes/
agentshield-reports/
# AI feature probe state (holds a throwaway test account)
scripts/.ai_probe_user.json

# ── The marketing website ships separately ───────────────────────────
# The source repository publishes the agent, API, warehouse, exports and
# the app UI (`web/`). The static marketing/checkout site (`website/`) is
# deployed on its own (Vercel/Netlify, see docs/FRONTENDS.md) and is NOT
# part of this repository (ADR-023).
website/

# ── Live deployment progress ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The Azure VM progress log tracks a live billing server (domains, tokens
# handling, rebuild notes). Operational detail - keep it out of the repo.
docs/deployment/azure-vm-progress.md

